---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { GITHUB_MOD, KSP_VERSION, PRODUCT } from '../consts';
---

<PageLayout
	title="Get started"
	description="How to prepare for KSC Tower Network as a pilot, controller, spectator, or tower operator."
>
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="shell">
			<h1>Get started</h1>
			<p>
				A public player ZIP and always-on community tower are still being prepared. Here is
				the honest setup path so you know what to expect when {PRODUCT} goes live.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="prose">
				<h2>Requirements</h2>
			</div>
			<ul class="checklist" style="max-width: 42rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
				<li>Kerbal Space Program {KSP_VERSION} (Windows x64 for the bundled voice bridge).</li>
				<li>Module Manager (required dependency).</li>
				<li>The community player ZIP (tower host is already baked in) — or a self-hosted build if you run your own tower.</li>
				<li>Recommended: ClickThroughBlocker so tower panels do not click through to the craft.</li>
			</ul>

			<div class="prose">
				<h2>If you want to fly</h2>
				<p>
					When the release pack ships, drop <code>GameData/KSCTowerNetwork/</code> into
					your KSP install and launch. Pair the plugin with a short code from the web app,
					tune the in-game radio (TWR 122.0 / GND 121.7 / EMRG 121.5), and talk on PTT
					(default <code>R</code>). Telemetry streams while the beacon is on; other pilots
					appear as ghosts in your world, not as shared vessels.
				</p>
				<p>
					Until that ZIP is published, follow the open repository and wait for a tagged
					release.
				</p>
				<div class="cta-row" style="margin: 1.25rem 0 2.5rem;">
					<a class="btn btn-primary" href={GITHUB_MOD} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"
						>View mod on GitHub</a
					>
					<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/how-it-works">Read the loop</a>
				</div>

				<h2>If you want to control</h2>
				<p>
					Controllers only need a browser and a signed-in account. No KSP install.
					Open the lobby, join the controller queue (“take next call”), or assume a vacant
					seat on an active radio channel. Work map, clearances, voice, ACARS, countdown,
					and the tower wall from there.
				</p>

				<h2>If you want to spectate</h2>
				<p>
					Sign in (guests are lobby-text only), hit Spectate on a room, and watch
					listen-only. You get ops audio without PTT, plus the booth side channel for
					spectator chatter the pilot does not hear. If your account can assume tower,
					you can take a vacant seat from there.
				</p>

				<h2>If you want to host</h2>
				<p>
					Operators stand up the API, web desk, and LiveKit project, choose signup policy,
					then run the packaging script so player builds point at those hosts. The mod
					repo documents env vars, CORS, MariaDB, Redis, and the release ZIP flow.
				</p>
				<p>
					Status right now: the product stack exists and is documented for production; this
					site is the public front door. The playable hosted tower endpoint is still being
					brought online.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</PageLayout>
